MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The alligator clip leads and heat shrink fit the practical connection work suggested by my breadboards, PCB supplies, battery holder, and relay module: making temporary connections and insulating finished wiring.",
    "The component tester feels useful because it would help me check parts for my circuit projects, and assembling the kit fits my interest in hands-on electronics."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The waveform generator and temperature controller require needs I have not shown: working on circuits does not mean I need waveform generation, and measuring temperature does not mean I need to control heating or cooling.",
    "The structural cable, nut assortment, and oil lack a specific job connecting them to what I want now. The magnet wire is relevant to my toroid cores, but a full pound is more than I would choose without a planned winding project."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any electronics equipment, even when its purpose goes beyond the connection and component work in my history.",
    "My occasional practical purchases seem to have been stretched into a general need for hardware and maintenance supplies, without evidence that I need those particular materials or sizes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Immediate usefulness matters: I am more likely to choose something that helps connect, insulate, or check the small circuits suggested by my past purchases than something requiring a new project.",
    "A related item can still be premature. I would need a winding plan before buying a large spool of magnet wire and would check my meter's connections before choosing replacement test leads."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on circuit interests, but sometimes treated a related tool or material as evidence of a current need."
}
